 "comment": "Android SMS Stealer and Dropper disguised as \"RTO Challan\" app. Spreads via SMS worming/smishing.\r\n\r\nTechnical Analysis:\r\n\r\nEntry: Receiver intercepts SMS and passes execution to a decoy launcher hidden in a fake library path (androidx.emoji2.text.m).\r\n\r\nPersistence: Abuses BIND_VPN_SERVICE to launch a persistent \"Fake VPN\" service (com.eksctm.android.ServiceHandler) that prevents system kill.\r\n\r\nDropper: Contains REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES permission and code to write raw byte-buffers to disk (ServiceHandler.b), indicating it drops a secondary banking payload.\r\n\r\nObfuscation: Uses Control Flow Flattening and hides C2 configuration inside obfuscated resource files (res/values/kbfcb*.xml) rather than Java strings.",
